From: NWA50BE OpenWrt Project <noreply@invalid.example>
Subject: [PATCH] dropbear: backport 2026.92 and 2026.93 security fixes
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only

Add the security-relevant fixes of dropbear 2026.92 and 2026.93 to
2025.89 as patch files on top of 0029, instead of a version bump (OpenWrt
main took 2026.92 in 49096a9c48 and 2026.94 in e9a6e45556, which also
brings the whole 2026.90 feature set and a reworked patch stack).
Upstream commits: 8d8e1930 (a long authorized_keys line continued as a
new line, which could bypass restrictions such as command=), 23ec7828
(-t with -B), d35cf537 (unbounded KEX reply queue), 10d1b725 (permitopen
port range), edd5fa1e (packet length wraparound) and e968c1a6 with
08729e21 (scp progress meter filename escaping; the package builds scp
with SCPPROGRESS=1). Upstream CHANGES lists no CVE ids for them.
100-pubkey_path.patch is refreshed for the new offsets.
